  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Jérôme Valcke is a French sports administrator who became FIFA's secretary general after working in television journalism and sports marketing. He oversaw preparations for the World Cups in South Africa and Brazil before leaving the organisation. With his wife Ornella, he later owned Mas Igneus, a winery in Spain's Priorat region.",
