  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "French sports executive Jérôme Valcke negotiated international broadcasting rights before entering football administration. At Canal+, his responsibilities included buying sports coverage and developing Sport+, an agency that supplied the broadcaster and sold rights abroad. During the Barcelona and Atlanta Olympics, the channel devoted its output to round-the-clock coverage of the Games.\n\nAt FIFA, he advocated bringing media-rights sales into the organisation, expanding a commercial operation initially focused on sponsorship. Major markets were handled directly, while agencies continued to represent particular territories. This work required negotiations with broadcasters and intermediaries, alongside the government relationships involved in delivering international tournaments.",
    "html": "<p>French sports executive Jérôme Valcke negotiated international broadcasting rights before entering football administration. At Canal+, his responsibilities included buying sports coverage and developing Sport+, an agency that supplied the broadcaster and sold rights abroad. During the Barcelona and Atlanta Olympics, the channel devoted its output to round-the-clock coverage of the Games.</p>\r\n<p>At FIFA, he advocated bringing media-rights sales into the organisation, expanding a commercial operation initially focused on sponsorship. Major markets were handled directly, while agencies continued to represent particular territories. This work required negotiations with broadcasters and intermediaries, alongside the government relationships involved in delivering international tournaments.</p>\r\n",
